{"n": 216, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "216.webp", "text": "730 34125\n\n12—113\n\n1211604 CHECKING AND ADJUSTING\nIGNITION TIMING\n~ 4 Cylinder / M 10 —\n\nImportant!\n\nSee page 12 - 0 for instructions for working\non éngine electrical system.\n\nTesting Conditions:\n\nPluggable TDC sender installed.\n\nEngine at operating temperature — oi!\ntemperature at least 60° C (140° F),\nDistributor/DME control unit number**\nconforms with information on nominal value\nmicrofiche.\n\nConnect, BMW Service Tester or BMW Digital\nTester to operating instructions,\n\nCars with NOx Control:\n\nThe NOx control unit is series connected after\nthe ignition control unit as 2 second control\nunit. Function of NOx control has to be\nstopped to check the ignition timing,\n\nPull off 4.8 mm (0.189\") plug on 17° C\n\n(63° F) temperature switch and hold on\nground. E\n\nCheck / adjust ignition timing.\n\nAt engine speed of about 1500 rpm NOx con-\n\" will retard the ignition timing by approx.\n1\n\n** See Specifications\n\nChecking Dwell Angle:\n\nThe dwet! angle is given by design and can be\nchecked, but not adjusted.\n\nThe ignition control unit is no longer ready for\noperation in case of malfunction.\n\nChecking/Adjusting Ignition Timing*:\nPull off vacuum hose for advance control,\n\nStart and run engine at test speed*.\n\nCheck ignition timing? adjusting if necessary.\nCorrect by loosening screw and turning the\ndistributor accordingly.\n\n+ = ignition timing advanced\n\n— = ignition timing retarded\n\n* See Nominal Value Microfiche", "words": [["730", 0.1915, 0.5133, 0.2072, 0.5219], ["34125", 0.2118, 0.5139, 0.2411, 0.5225], ["12—113", 0.4574, 0.0245, 0.5527, 0.0491], ["1211604", 0.2614, 0.0683, 0.3095, 0.0796], ["CHECKING", 0.3232, 0.0683, 0.3799, 0.0796], ["AND", 0.384, 0.069, 0.4078, 0.0796], ["ADJUSTING", 0.4119, 0.069, 0.4742, 0.0796], ["IGNITION", 0.3232, 0.0842, 0.3739, 0.0955], ["TIMING", 0.3779, 0.0849, 0.4174, 0.0955], ["~", 0.3237, 0.1061, 0.3293, 0.1074], ["4", 0.33